interface.longDescription:
Local Commander lets ChatGPT work on your own Windows computer. It is for developers and technical users who want ChatGPT to look at a real project and act on it, not only suggest code.

With Local Commander, ChatGPT can:
- read and search the files of a folder you choose, and see its Git status, changes and history;
- run the commands you ask for, such as builds, tests, Git or PowerShell, and show you the real output;
- create and edit files in that folder;
- check a service running on your computer, such as a local web app's health page.

You stay in control. You choose which folders Local Commander can use, and writing files or running commands needs the permissions you set on your computer. Changes go through separate tools marked as write actions, so ChatGPT can ask you first. Local Commander cannot give itself more access or reach another account's computer.

Requirements: Windows 11 x64, Node.js 20 or later, and the Local Commander agent installed and paired with your account. The computer must be on and online while ChatGPT works on it.
